<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 7 April, from 529 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">529 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,497 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justinian promulgates the first Code of Roman law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Justinian issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a>, gathering imperial constitutions into a single authoritative collection. Revised in 534, it became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a> that shaped European law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1348">1348 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">678 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles IV founds the university in Prague</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a>, issued the charter founding a university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, the first in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a>. Now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-university">Charles University</a>, it later became a centre of the Hussite reform movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1739">1739 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">287 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Highwayman Dick Turpin is hanged at York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dick Turpin, convicted of horse theft, was hanged on the Knavesmire at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>. The violent robber was later romanticised in fiction as a dashing gentleman of the road.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1798">1798 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">228 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress creates the Mississippi Territory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Congress organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> Territory on land ceded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1795. It was later enlarged and divided into the states of Mississippi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1827">1827 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">199 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Walker records the first sale of friction matches</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stockton-on-Tees chemist John Walker sold his newly invented 'friction lights', matches struck against sandpaper. He never patented them, and others soon copied the idea.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy invades Albania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s forces landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a> and other ports, and within days <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">King Zog</a> had fled. Albania was joined to the Italian crown, and the invasion later served as a base for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Genocide against the Tutsi begins in Rwanda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hours after President Habyarimana's aircraft was shot down, extremists began killing Tutsi and moderate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a>. In about 100 days an estimated 500,000 to 800,000 people were murdered.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">Genocide</a></div></div></li></ol>
